# Two files here are CITED as evidence by proof.product.manualgen.board_preserved, so
# they are exempt while the rest of the directory stays ignored. Two gitignore rules
# had to be respected to make this work, both easy to get wrong:
#   1. git does not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so the rule above is
#      `reports/*` (contents) not `reports/` (the directory) -- a `!` negation under
#      an excluded directory is silently inert.
#   2. LATER RULES WIN, so these negations must come AFTER the exclusion, not before.
# Verify with `git check-ignore -v <file>`; do not assume.
!/docs/manuals/developer/manualgen/reports/mdo_226_validate_summary_v1.csv
!/docs/manuals/developer/manualgen/reports/mdo_226_build_dry_run_summary_v1.csv
